From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:40:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: make the desktop window at the session's start, and
 register its classes in every pseudo-process

A pseudo-process child could not create a window unless its parent had
already drawn one: get_desktop_window in the child found no desktop
window and could not make it, so NtUserCreateWindowEx failed with
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED. On a Wine host explorer makes the desktop window
when the session starts; on iOS the first CreateWindowEx of the first
process did. init_user (run once, for the session) now makes it right
after registering the desktop classes. wineserver also keeps window
classes per process, and init_user registered the desktop and message
classes for the first process only: NtUserInitializeClientPfnArrays,
which user32 calls once per process, now registers them for every later
process, as register_builtin_classes already does for the controls.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-child-process.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/win32u-unix/class_ios.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/class_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/class_ios.c
index 1a30ac6..bf802d6 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/class_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/class_ios.c
@@ -391,6 +391,11 @@ static void init_user(void)
     sysparams_init();
     winstation_init();
     register_desktop_class();
+    /* Playport: the session's first process makes the desktop window now, as
+     * explorer does at a Wine session's start. A pseudo-process child cannot
+     * make it (get_desktop_window failed there with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED), so a
+     * child whose parent had drawn no window could create none. */
+    get_desktop_window();
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
@@ -446,7 +451,23 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtUserInitializeClientPfnArrays( const ntuser_client_func_ptr *c
     }
     pthread_mutex_unlock( &winproc_lock );
 
-    pthread_once( &init_once, init_user );
+    {
+        /* Playport: init_user runs once, for the session, and registers the
+         * desktop and message window classes with it; wineserver keeps window
+         * classes per process. A pseudo-process child had neither, so when no
+         * desktop window existed yet, get_desktop_window could not make one
+         * (grab_class) and NtUserCreateWindowEx failed with
+         * ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED. Every later process registers them itself, as
+         * register_builtin_classes already does for the controls. */
+        static void *init_peb;
+        if (!init_peb) init_peb = peb;
+        pthread_once( &init_once, init_user );
+        if (peb != init_peb)
+        {
+            register_desktop_class();
+            dprintf(2, "[pfn] peb=%p registered the desktop and message classes\n", peb);
+        }
+    }
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
